# 20. Required Security Tests

Do not simply modify code and assume it is secure.

After implementation, test at minimum:

## Tenant isolation

Attempt to access Tenant B resources while authenticated as Tenant A.

Expected:

```text
DENIED
```

## Role escalation

Attempt to change:

```text
role
permissions
tenant_id
user_id
```

through client requests.

Expected:

```text
DENIED
```

## Direct endpoint access

Attempt to call sensitive backend functions directly without the appropriate permission.

Expected:

```text
DENIED
```

## Manipulated financial values

Attempt to submit modified:

```text
amount
balance
quantity
price
tenant_id
account_id
```

Expected:

```text
SERVER VALIDATES AND REJECTS INVALID/UNAUTHORIZED VALUES
```

## Duplicate transactions

Replay the same financial request.

Expected:

```text
ONE AUTHORITATIVE TRANSACTION
```

## Offline replay

Create an offline operation and replay it multiple times after reconnecting.

Expected:

```text
NO DUPLICATE FINANCIAL POSTING
```

## Unauthorized audit modification

Attempt to modify/delete audit records as an ordinary user.

Expected:

```text
DENIED
```

## Frontend manipulation

Modify:

* React state
* localStorage
* route parameters
* request payloads
* client-side role values
* UI visibility

Expected:

```text
NO PRIVILEGE ESCALATION
```

